<p>The United States won the men’s ice hockey gold medal at the Milan-Cortina Winter Olympics on Sunday, beating Canada 2–1 in overtime after Jack Hughes scored the sudden-death winner. The win gave the U.S. men their first Olympic hockey gold since 1980—and their third men’s title overall. The cross-border rivalry drew huge attention, from packed watch parties to a rush of postgame reaction. Some of it spilled into online political symbolism after official U.S. accounts weighed in.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/sHYBA2O8XuEK6ojKCG-c4ch5TWjKYq27dBEGmowA0LKSeHl9pFDwBD9KhjxBu0bjzVkdNJHgEsJYOHRHpGGODRSoEycfYUQa-zqGzOIqn-CT-goT36HlPtv8Qe9lk-z4hUfZJ6D9i78eiYZrL15aeINNO0hqp4sqglTDqg62buRS49NaIK89KT8MgLYt8OzrNt8kjQn78bBg4rFQJMKkdHvZDDqddnWwTLQs' alt='Players celebrate after the United States beat Canada 2–1 in overtime to win men’s Olympic hockey gold in Milan-Cortina.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Rivalry watch parties: In Toronto, NYT reported that more than 300 fans packed The Pilot bar starting at 7:30 a.m. to watch the final on big screens.</li><li>Overtime detail: AllSides reported that the U.S. forced overtime, then Hughes scored early in the extra period to beat Canadian goaltender Jordan Binnington for the winner.</li><li>White House post context: Firstpost said many viewed the eagle-over-goose image as a pointed response to Justin Trudeau’s earlier “you can’t take our game” remark, while Al Jazeera reported some Canadians denounced the graphic as disrespectful rather than friendly banter.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>White House: Posted an image widely interpreted as an eagle towering over a Canadian goose after the U.S. overtime win—something some read as a pointed reply to earlier Canadian remarks. (<a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/after-us-hockey-win-white-house-posts-eagle-towering-over-canadian-goose-13982553.html'>Firstpost</a>)</li><li>Canadian critics of the post: Some Canadians objected to the White House illustration, calling it disrespectful rather than friendly sporting banter. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/22/white-house-post-after-us-hockey-win-over-canada-stirs-controversy'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Fans in Canada and U.S.: Many fans treated the final as a high-stakes rivalry game first, turning out in large numbers at bars and watch parties, while politics faded into the background at puck drop. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/22/world/europe/us-canada-hockey-gold-medal-olympics.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/nation/u-s-mens-hockey-beats-canada-in-ot-to-win-first-olympic-gold-medal-since-1980'>U.S. men&#x27;s hockey beats Canada in OT to win first Olympic gold medal since 1980</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/us-hockey-canada-milano-cortina-winter-olympics-gold-medal/'>U.S. beats Canada in thrilling hockey finals to win Olympic gold</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/22/world/canada/2026-olympics-hockey-canada-united-states.html'>Fans Pack Bars as U.S.-Canada Hockey Game Puts Rivalry on the Line</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/after-us-hockey-win-white-house-posts-eagle-towering-over-canadian-goose-13982553.html'>Digital diplomacy or sporting banter? After US hockey win, White House posts eagle towering over Canadian goose</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/22/white-house-post-after-us-hockey-win-over-canada-stirs-controversy'>White House post after US hockey win over Canada stirs controversy</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-02-22-0800/sports-team-usa-mens-hockey-wins-gold-medal-overtime-against-canada-winter-olympics'>Team USA men&#x27;s hockey wins gold medal in overtime against Canada at Winter Olympics</a> - allsides.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nbclosangeles.com/olympics/2026-milan-cortina/team-usa-canada-mens-hockey-gold-medal-game/3851942/'>The United States defeats Canada 2–1 during overtime, winning gold in the men&#x27;s tournament in ice hockey for the first time since 1980, exactly 46 years after the Miracle on Ice.</a> - nbclosangeles.com</li></ul>